==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
This stage is easy if done correctly: bring [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to rush this stage. Just deploy stallers until you can afford him, then deploy more stallers, and destroy the base. The Zang Roo is not a threat, as it just burrows past your units, allowing Awakened Bahamut to finish the base off.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
Stalling is even easier with the [[Barrier]] from UltraBaaBaa, and even multiple [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cats]] can be stacked before breaking it with a [[Barrier Breaker]] or the [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast Cannon]]. Most of the Zombies except for Zamelle will burrow as soon as the base is hit, which means remaining enemies can be burst down. If not rushing it plays like a standard Zombie stage, just with more Zuches than usual that need to be intercepted.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
It is very easy to rush the initial wave of enemies that appear alongside the boss with [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]. Simply give him a clear shot to the enemy base and let him handle the rest, then, once the smoke clears, it'll just be Wild Doges and Zang Roos. You can deal with them using [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cats]] and [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cats]].

